---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getProjects } from "../lib/projects";
import { computeStats } from "../lib/stats";

const projects = await getProjects();
const stats = computeStats(projects);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — projectopensource.org"
  description="Yuvan Adarsh Jagannathan — CS student rebuilding AI subscriptions as open-source tools."
  footerVariant="about"
>
  <div style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(64px,9vw,120px) clamp(20px,5vw,72px) clamp(64px,9vw,120px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 320px;gap:56px;align-items:start">
    <div>
      <p style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin:0 0 20px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-accent)">
        <span style="width:44px;height:1px;background:var(--color-accent)"></span>About
      </p>
      <h1 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(34px,4.4vw,58px);letter-spacing:-0.025em">
        Yuvan Adarsh Jagannathan
      </h1>

      <div style="margin-top:28px;font-size:16px;max-width:60ch;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 84%, transparent)">
        <p>
          I'm a computer science student. Somewhere between my third and
          fourth AI subscription I did the arithmetic, didn't like it, and
          started rebuilding the tools instead of renting them.
        </p>
        <p>
          The pattern is always the same. The demo is magic, the model is a
          public API, and the twenty dollars is buying glue code plus a nice
          onboarding flow. That glue is worth something — it's just not
          worth a subscription I forget to cancel. So I write the glue, put
          it on GitHub, and document the parts that are still bad.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of these are startups. Nothing here has a pricing page. If a
          build stops working I'll mark it archived rather than pretend,
          and if you want to take one over, the license already says you
          can.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,auto);gap:40px;margin-top:48px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-divider)">
        <div>
          <p style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:var(--font-heading-weight);font-size:28px">
            {stats.toolsRebuilt}
          </p>
          <p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, transparent)">
            Tools rebuilt
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:var(--font-heading-weight);font-size:28px">
            ${stats.subscriptionsReplacedPerYear.toLocaleString()}
          </p>
          <p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, transparent)">
            Replaced / year
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-heading);font-weight:var(--font-heading-weight);font-size:28px">
            {stats.githubStars}
          </p>
          <p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, transparent)">
            GitHub stars
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="card elev-sm">
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 60%, transparent)">
        Elsewhere
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/posrc"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
        style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;text-decoration:none;color:var(--color-text);font-size:13.5px"
      >
        <span>GitHub</span>
        <span style="font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 65%, transparent)">
          @posrc
        </span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://instagram.com/yuvanadarsh"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
        style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;text-decoration:none;color:var(--color-text);font-size:13.5px"
      >
        <span>Instagram</span>
        <span style="font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 65%, transparent)">
          @yuvanadarsh
        </span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://linkedin.com/in/yuvanadarsh"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
        style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;text-decoration:none;color:var(--color-text);font-size:13.5px"
      >
        <span>LinkedIn</span>
        <span style="font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 65%, transparent)">
          yuvanadarsh
        </span>
      </a>
      <p style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 52%, transparent)">
        Instagram is where the build clips go. GitHub is where the actual
        work is.
      </p>
      <hr class="hr" style="margin:8px 0" />
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">See the builds</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
